.DS_Store
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
src/demiurge-launcher-rs/target/

# NEPTR binary assets (111MB of wav): needed on disk by the standalone/plugin
# and the Pi, but they never change and do not belong in git history.
neptr/samples/drumloops/
# neptr/csound/ir/ is NO LONGER IGNORED (2026-10-02).
# These 25 impulse responses (15 MB) are a HARD dependency: csound aborts at
# init with "soundin cannot open .../ir/11_spring_short_flat.wav" and the
# instrument does not start. They existed only on this Mac -- not in git, not on
# a remote, not in any backup -- which is the same exposure that cost a full
# rebuild when the Pi's SD card died on 2026-10-01. The NAM profiles next door
# are tracked at 7.1 MB, so there is no size argument for treating these
# differently. Tracking them is what makes a rebuild self-contained.

# Rig backup kit (setup-script/backup-rig.sh). latest/ is TRACKED on purpose:
# it is the seed the installer restores from after a card death. The dated
# tarballs duplicate it, so they stay out of git history.
rig-backup/*/snapshots/
rig-backup/snapshots/

# MAME artwork only. Arcade ROMs are tracked (EMGOR approved, 2026-10-25,
# private repo only).
demiurge/games/system/mame/artwork/

# --- sync / local split (demiurge/SYNC_LOCAL.md) -------------------------------
# HARD RULE: demiurge/sync/** ships to every Pi; demiurge/local/** NEVER leaves
# this box through THIS repo. Only the two placeholders are tracked so the
# directories exist in a fresh clone. demiurge/local/ is the root of the node's
# OWN separate git repo (setup-script/node-repo/), which is how local state is
# versioned without ever touching the shared repo.
demiurge/local/*
!demiurge/local/.gitkeep
!demiurge/local/README.md
# (demiurge/sync/** is intentionally not listed: it is tracked.)
